/// llvm —— LLVM IR 方言的领域描述（corpus，不是最终语法）。
///
/// 上游：mlir/include/mlir/Dialect/LLVMIR/LLVMOps.td +
/// LLVMIntrinsicOps.td（含 LLVMOpBase.td / LLVMAttrDefs.td / LLVMEnums.td 闭包）。
/// 只有领域事实：部件、约束、文本、语义。没有 namespace/class/builder。
///
/// 范围与计数：dialect-coverage.py 以 `llvm-tblgen --dump-json` 的 opName 为准，
/// 上游 323 个、本文件 323 条，严格集合相等（missing=0, extra=0）。opName 就是
/// 打印助记符（含 `intr.` 前缀），所以语料声明名与上游逐字相同，不做后缀对齐；
/// 一条语料 op 只对应一条上游记录。
///
/// 通道分布（按 escape-audit 的继承解析，即 op 经 `from` 取到 schema 的通道）：
/// block 256（其中 10 条带 `custom<>` 钩子）、Generic 59、Custom 8、Gap 0。
/// dialect-corpus.py 的 text-channels 表把任何带 `from` 的 op 记作 block，
/// 因此它的表显示 284/8/31：多出的 28 条是从 Generic schema 继承了通道的 op
/// （VectorReduceInt 9、VPReduceInt 9、VPReduceFloat 6、VPBinaryInt 4）。
///
/// 同名助记符字符串不等于同一个 op（重要）：
///   严格口径下 `tblgen` 的 opName 已经区分了核心 op 与 intrinsic：核心加法是
///   `add`，向量谓词归约是 `intr.vp.reduce.add`，向量归约是
///   `intr.vector.reduce.add`。三者是三条上游记录，本文件也分别声明，不再有
///   “只声明其中一种形态、另一种记进 Doc”的偏差。同理 `fadd`/`fmul`（核心）与
///   `intr.experimental.constrained.fadd`/`intr.vector.reduce.fadd` 各自独立。
///   `intr.vp.merge` 的基类 `LLVM_VPSelectBase` 用 `"vp." # mnem` 拼助记符，
///   上游 opName 是 `intr.vp.merge`；此前的 `intr.merge` 是错误拼写，已改名。
///
/// 文本通道：所有 assemblyFormat 逐字转写；`$x` → `x`，`type($x)` → `type(x)`，
/// `(fastmath `` $x^)?` → `if x { "fastmath" x }`，`oilist(...)` → `oilist(...)`，
/// `prop-dict` 只在打印 properties 的 op 上出现（load/store/atomicrmw/cmpxchg/
/// masked.load/gather/store/scatter）。
///
/// 新增族的通道依据（逐条核对 tblgen 的 assemblyFormat 字段）：
///   - 核心 `add`/`mul`：`$lhs, $rhs ($overflowFlags^)? attr-dict : type($res)`
///     （LLVMOps.td:59-71、add :156、mul :159）→ block。
///   - 核心 `sdiv`/`udiv`：`(`exact` $isExact^)? $lhs, $rhs attr-dict : type($res)`
///     （:78-94；sdiv :163、udiv :161）→ block；上游是 ConditionallySpeculatable，
///     故只记 no_memory_effect，不冒充 pure。
///   - 核心 `srem`/`urem`：`$lhs, $rhs attr-dict : type($res)`（:165、:168）→ block。
///   - 核心 `and`/`xor`：同无 flag 形态（:171、:175）→ block；`or` 多
///     `(`disjoint` $isDisjoint^)?`（:96-113、:172）→ block。
///   - 核心 `fadd`/`fmul`：`$lhs, $rhs (fastmath^)? attr-dict : type($res)`
///     （:116-132；fadd :245、fmul :247）→ block。
///   - 核心 `fneg`：`$operand (fastmath^)? attr-dict : type($res)`
///     （LLVM_UnaryFloatArithmeticOp :134-146；记录 LLVM_FNegOp :250）→ block。
///   - `intr.trunc`：`(operands) (fastmath^)? attr-dict :
///     functional-type(operands, results)`（LLVM_FTruncOp :175 经
///     LLVM_UnaryIntrOpF :32-40）→ block，套 IntrinsicWithFastmath。
///   - `intr.{smax,smin,umax,umin}`（:227-230）与
///     `intr.{sadd,uadd,ssub,usub,sshl,ushl}.sat`（:902-907）：都经
///     LLVM_BinarySameArgsIntrOpI/Base（:41-50、:53-56），格式
///     `(operands) attr-dict : functional-type(operands, results)` → block。
///   - `intr.experimental.constrained.*` 共 49 条，**全部有 assemblyFormat**
///     （LLVMIntrinsicOps.td:502 起，族内基类与各 op 的 override），没有一条
///     Generic。分形态：
///       * 一元带 rm（LLVM_ConstrainedUnaryIntrRM :597，fmt :601）：
///         sqrt/sin/cos/tan/asin/acos/atan/sinh/cosh/tanh/exp/exp2/log/log10/
///         log2/rint/nearbyint（记录 :777-793）；
///       * 一元无 rm（:609，fmt :613）：ceil/floor/round/roundeven/trunc
///         （:796-800）；
///       * 二元带 rm（:621，fmt :625）：pow/atan2（:803-804）；fadd/fsub/fmul/
///         fdiv/frem 各有 override 的同一形态（:709-751）；
///       * 二元无 rm（:633，fmt :637）：maxnum/minnum/maximum/minimum（:807-810）；
///       * 三元带 rm（fma :754、fmuladd :763，fmt :758/:767）；
///       * powi/ldexp（:812/:822，fmt :816/:826）用 functional-type；
///       * FP→int 带 rm（:644，fmt :648）：lrint/llrint（:833-834）；
///         FP→int 无 rm（:656，fmt :660）：lround/llround/fptosi/fptoui（:835-840）；
///       * 单操作数转换 `type($arg_0) `to` type(results)`：uitofp :846、
///         sitofp :855、fptrunc :864（带 rm）；fpext :873（无 rm）；
///       * fcmp/fcmps（LLVM_ConstrainedFCmpIntrBase :667，fmt :686）：
///         `$predicate $arg_0, $arg_1 $fpExceptionBehavior ... : type($arg_0)`。
///   - `intr.vector.reduce.*` 共 17 条，分三种上游形态：
///       * I 族 9 条 add/and/mul/or/smax/smin/umax/umin/xor
///         （LLVM_VecReductionI，:1303-1306、:1328-1336）**没有 assemblyFormat**
///         → Generic；
///       * F 族 6 条 fmax/fmin/fmaximum/fminimum/fmaximumnum/fminimumnum
///         （LLVM_VecReductionF，:1292-1301、:1338-1343）有
///         `(operands) (fastmath^)? attr-dict : functional-type(operands, results)`
///         → block；
///       * Acc 族 2 条 fadd/fmul（LLVM_VecReductionAccBase，:1310-1323、
///         :1345-1346）有同一形态 → block。
///
/// 钩子（钩子名恰好是上游 `custom<...>`）：CmpPredicate(icmp/fcmp)；
/// InsertExtractValueElementType(extractvalue/insertvalue)；ShuffleType；
/// GEPIndices；SwitchOpCases；IndirectBrOpSucessors（上游拼写如此）；
/// OpBundles(assume)；LLVMLinkage(mlir.ifunc)。实参与上游逐位对应。
///
/// Custom 依据（上游 hasCustomAssemblyFormat = 1）：
///   alloca(LLVMOps.td:296)、invoke(:805)、landingpad(:822)、call(:952)、
///   mlir.global(:1658)、mlir.alias(:1811)、func(:2274)、call_intrinsic(:2781)。
///
/// 事实：只用 fact-glossary 的 core 词。Pure → pure；Commutative → commutative；
/// Terminator → terminator；ConstantLike → constant_like；ReturnLike → return_like；
/// NoMemoryEffect → no_memory_effect；MemoryEffects 读写/分配 →
/// memory_effect(read|write|allocate)；SameOperandsAndResultType / AllTypesMatch →
/// same_type；SameOperandsAndResultElementType → same_element_type；Symbol/SymbolName
/// → symbol；SymbolTable → symbol_table；SymbolVisibility → symbol_visibility；
/// IsolatedFromAbove → isolated_from_above；AutomaticAllocationScope →
/// automatic_allocation_scope；AffineScope → affine_scope；NoTerminator →
/// no_terminator；NoRegionArguments → no_region_args；SingleBlockImplicitTerminator
/// → single_block + implicit_terminator(return)；AttrSizedOperandSegments →
/// operand_segments_by_attribute。没有方言本地事实。
///
/// 只写进 Doc 的语义（文法没有对应谓词，或 core 词表达不了条件性）：
///   - `sdiv`/`udiv`/`srem`/`urem`：上游是 ConditionallySpeculatable 而非 Pure；
///     核心词 speculatable 表达不了“条件性”，故只记 no_memory_effect 与类型关系。
///   - constrained `fcmp`/`fcmps`：结果的 i1 元素类型与操作数同形状由
///     TypesMatchWith 表达，这里只记 same_type(arg_0, arg_1)，形状关系写进 Doc。
///   - `powi`/`ldexp`：上游 overloadedOperands 指定了重载操作数下标（powi 无、
///     ldexp 为 [1]），文法不记下标，只在 Doc 说明。
///   - verifier/接口语义：load/store 的 alignment 与原子性约束；
///     alloca 的 elem_type 与结果指针元素类型一致；GEP 的 inrange 只用于常量；
///     call/invoke 的 callee 与 var_callee_type 一致；atomicrmw 的 bin_op 决定
///     结果类型；cmpxchg 结果是 {T, i1} 结构；switch 的 case_operand_segments
///     与 caseDestinations 一一对应；func 的 body 入口参数与 function_type 一致。
///
/// GAP：无。未使用 Gap 构造。

dialect llvm {
  Doc "LLVM IR dialect: SSA form of LLVM IR with LLVM-compatible types, memory, calls, atomics, coroutines and intrinsics.";

  // ---- 类型 ----

  type_def ptr {
    Doc "LLVM pointer type (!llvm.ptr<addrspace>); address space defaults to 0 and is then not printed.";
    Parameters (address_space: i64 = 0);
    Assembly { if address_space { "<" address_space ">" } }
  }
  type_def struct {
    Doc "LLVM struct type: an optional name and a body, printed by the hand-written printer (LLVMTypes.cpp); a literal struct is !llvm.struct<(T0, T1, ...)>.";
    Parameters (name: optional<string>, body: array<type>);
    Assembly   Custom;
  }
  type_def array {
    Doc "LLVM array type (!llvm.array<N x T>).";
    Parameters (element: type, count: i64);
    Assembly { "<" count "x" custom<PrettyLLVMType>(element) ">" }
  }
  type_def metadata {
    Doc "LLVM metadata type (!llvm.metadata), the SSA carrier of metadata attributes; it is a trivial C++ type (LLVMTypes.h:70), not an ODS TypeDef.";
    Assembly   Modeled;   /* 没有 ODS 记录：Generic/Custom 都无法被上游证伪 */
  }

  constraint llvm_type = integer | float | ptr | struct | array | metadata | token | vector | function_type;
  constraint llvm_scalar = integer | float;
  constraint llvm_ptr = ptr | vector;
  constraint aggregate = struct | array;

  enum FastmathFlags: bits {
    Doc "Floating-point fast-math flags; empty prints nothing.";
    Cases [ none = 0, nnan = 1, ninf = 2, nsz = 4, arcp = 8, contract = 16,
             afn = 32, reassoc = 64 ];
    Groups [ fast = reassoc | nnan | ninf | nsz | arcp | contract | afn ];
  }

  enum IntegerOverflowFlags: bits {
    Doc "Integer overflow flags on arithmetic and trunc.";
    Cases [ none = 0, nsw = 1, nuw = 2 ];
  }

  enum AtomicOrdering {
    Doc "LLVM atomic ordering.";
    Cases [ not_atomic = 0, unordered = 1, monotonic = 2, acquire = 4,
             release = 5, acq_rel = 6, seq_cst = 7 ];
  }

  enum AtomicBinOp {
    Doc "Operation of llvm.atomicrmw.";
    Cases [ xchg = 0, add = 1, sub = 2, _and = 3, nand = 4, _or = 5,
             _xor = 6, max = 7, min = 8, umax = 9, umin = 10, fadd = 11,
             fsub = 12, fmax = 13, fmin = 14, uinc_wrap = 15, udec_wrap = 16,
             usub_cond = 17, usub_sat = 18, fmaximum = 19, fminimum = 20,
             fmaximumnum = 21, fminimumnum = 22 ];
  }

  enum Linkage {
    Doc "LLVM linkage kinds.";
    Cases [ external = 0, available_externally = 1, linkonce = 2,
             linkonce_odr = 3, weak = 4, weak_odr = 5, appending = 6,
             internal = 7, private = 8, extern_weak = 9, common = 10 ];
  }

  enum CConv {
    Doc "Calling conventions.";
    Cases [ ccc = 0, fastcc = 8, coldcc = 9, cc_10 = 10, cc_11 = 11,
             anyregcc = 13, preserve_mostcc = 14, preserve_allcc = 15,
             swiftcc = 16, cxx_fast_tlscc = 17, tailcc = 18,
             cfguard_checkcc = 19, swifttailcc = 20, preserve_nonecc = 21,
             x86_stdcallcc = 64, x86_fastcallcc = 65, arm_apcscc = 66,
             arm_aapcscc = 67, arm_aapcs_vfpcc = 68, msp430_intrcc = 69,
             x86_thiscallcc = 70, ptx_kernelcc = 71, ptx_devicecc = 72,
             spir_funccc = 75, spir_kernelcc = 76, intel_ocl_bicc = 77,
             x86_64_sysvcc = 78, win64cc = 79, x86_vectorcallcc = 80,
             hhvmcc = 81, hhvm_ccc = 82, x86_intrcc = 83, avr_intrcc = 84,
             avr_builtincc = 86, amdgpu_vscc = 87, amdgpu_gscc = 88,
             amdgpu_cscc = 90, amdgpu_kernelcc = 91, x86_regcallcc = 92,
             amdgpu_hscc = 93, msp430_builtincc = 94, amdgpu_lscc = 95,
             amdgpu_escc = 96, aarch64_vectorcallcc = 97,
             aarch64_sve_vectorcallcc = 98, wasm_emscripten_invokecc = 99,
             amdgpu_gfxcc = 100, m68k_intrcc = 101 ];
  }

  enum TailCallKind {
    Doc "Tail call kinds.";
    Cases [ none = 0, tail = 1, musttail = 2, notail = 3 ];
  }

  enum Visibility {
    Doc "Symbol visibility.";
    Cases [ Default = 0, hidden = 1, protected = 2 ];
  }

  enum UnnamedAddr {
    Doc "unnamed_addr kinds.";
    Cases [ None = 0, local_unnamed_addr = 1, unnamed_addr = 2 ];
  }

  enum RoundingMode {
    Doc "Rounding modes of the constrained FP intrinsics (LLVMEnums.td:776-808).";
    Cases [ towardzero = 0, tonearest = 1, upward = 2, downward = 3,
             tonearestaway = 4, dynamic = 7, invalid = -1 ];
  }

  enum FPExceptionBehavior {
    Doc "Exception behaviors of the constrained FP intrinsics (LLVMEnums.td:837-854).";
    Cases [ ignore = 0, maytrap = 1, strict = 2 ];
  }

  // ---- 整数/浮点算术与比较 ----

  schema IntBinaryWithOverflow {
    Doc "Integer binary arithmetic with optional nsw/nuw flags; operands and result share one type (LLVM_IntArithmeticOpWithOverflowFlag, LLVMOps.td:59).";
    Operands   (lhs: integer, rhs: integer);
    Results    (res: integer);
    Attributes (overflow_flags: IntegerOverflowFlags = none);
    Properties [pure, no_memory_effect, same_type(lhs, rhs), same_type(rhs, res)];
    Assembly   { lhs "," rhs if overflow_flags { overflow_flags }
                 attr-dict ":" type(res) }
  }

  schema IntBinaryWithExact {
    Doc "Integer binary arithmetic with an optional exact marker (LLVM_IntArithmeticOpWithExactFlag, LLVMOps.td:78).";
    Operands   (lhs: integer, rhs: integer);
    Results    (res: integer);
    Attributes (exact: optional<unit>);
    Properties [pure, no_memory_effect, same_type(lhs, rhs), same_type(rhs, res)];
    Assembly   { if exact { "exact" } lhs "," rhs attr-dict ":" type(res) }
  }

  schema FloatBinary {
    Doc "Floating-point binary arithmetic with optional fastmath flags (LLVM_FloatArithmeticOp, LLVMOps.td:116).";
    Operands   (lhs: float, rhs: float);
    Results    (res: float);
    Attributes (fastmathFlags: FastmathFlags = none);
    Properties [pure, no_memory_effect, same_type(lhs, rhs), same_type(rhs, res)];
    Assembly   { lhs "," rhs if fastmathFlags { "fastmath" fastmathFlags }
                 attr-dict ":" type(res) }
  }

  schema IntBinary {
    Doc "Integer binary arithmetic without flags; operands and result share one type (LLVM_IntArithmeticOp, LLVMOps.td:51). Speculatability is stated per op: and/xor are Pure, while srem/urem are only ConditionallySpeculatable upstream.";
    Operands   (lhs: integer, rhs: integer);
    Results    (res: integer);
    Properties [no_memory_effect, same_type(lhs, rhs), same_type(rhs, res)];
    Assembly   { lhs "," rhs attr-dict ":" type(res) }
  }

  schema IntBinaryWithDisjoint {
    Doc "Integer binary arithmetic with an optional disjoint marker (LLVM_IntArithmeticOpWithDisjointFlag, LLVMOps.td:96).";
    Operands   (lhs: integer, rhs: integer);
    Results    (res: integer);
    Attributes (disjoint: optional<unit>);
    Properties [pure, no_memory_effect, same_type(lhs, rhs), same_type(rhs, res)];
    Assembly   { if disjoint { "disjoint" } lhs "," rhs attr-dict ":" type(res) }
  }

  schema IntBinaryWithExactConditional {
    Doc "Integer binary arithmetic with an optional exact marker whose speculatability is conditional upstream (LLVM_IntArithmeticOpWithExactFlag with ConditionallySpeculatable, LLVMOps.td:78, 161-164). Pure is deliberately not claimed.";
    Operands   (lhs: integer, rhs: integer);
    Results    (res: integer);
    Attributes (exact: optional<unit>);
    Properties [no_memory_effect, same_type(lhs, rhs), same_type(rhs, res)];
    Assembly   { if exact { "exact" } lhs "," rhs attr-dict ":" type(res) }
  }

  op add from IntBinaryWithOverflow {
    Doc "Integer addition with optional nuw/nsw flags (LLVM_AddOp, LLVMOps.td:156).";
    Properties [commutative];
  }

  op sub from IntBinaryWithOverflow {
    Doc "Integer subtraction; optional nuw/nsw flags.";
  }

  op mul from IntBinaryWithOverflow {
    Doc "Integer multiplication with optional nuw/nsw flags (LLVM_MulOp, LLVMOps.td:159).";
    Properties [commutative];
  }

  op shl from IntBinaryWithOverflow {
    Doc "Integer left shift; optional nuw/nsw flags.";
  }

  op lshr from IntBinaryWithExact {
    Doc "Logical (unsigned) integer right shift with optional exact.";
  }

  op ashr from IntBinaryWithExact {
    Doc "Arithmetic (signed) integer right shift with optional exact.";
  }

  op udiv from IntBinaryWithExactConditional {
    Doc "Unsigned integer division with optional exact (LLVM_UDivOp, LLVMOps.td:161); upstream marks it ConditionallySpeculatable, not Pure.";
  }

  op sdiv from IntBinaryWithExactConditional {
    Doc "Signed integer division with optional exact (LLVM_SDivOp, LLVMOps.td:163); upstream marks it ConditionallySpeculatable, not Pure.";
  }

  op urem from IntBinary {
    Doc "Unsigned integer remainder (LLVM_URemOp, LLVMOps.td:165); upstream marks it ConditionallySpeculatable, not Pure.";
  }

  op srem from IntBinary {
    Doc "Signed integer remainder (LLVM_SRemOp, LLVMOps.td:168); upstream marks it ConditionallySpeculatable, not Pure.";
  }

  op and from IntBinary {
    Doc "Bitwise AND of two integers (LLVM_AndOp, LLVMOps.td:171).";
    Properties [pure];
  }

  op or from IntBinaryWithDisjoint {
    Doc "Bitwise OR of two integers with an optional disjoint marker (LLVM_OrOp, LLVMOps.td:172).";
  }

  op xor from IntBinary {
    Doc "Bitwise XOR of two integers (LLVM_XOrOp, LLVMOps.td:175).";
    Properties [pure];
  }

  op fadd from FloatBinary {
    Doc "Floating-point addition (LLVM_FAddOp, LLVMOps.td:245).";
  }

  op fmul from FloatBinary {
    Doc "Floating-point multiplication (LLVM_FMulOp, LLVMOps.td:247).";
  }

  op fsub from FloatBinary {
    Doc "Floating-point subtraction.";
  }

  op fdiv from FloatBinary {
    Doc "Floating-point division.";
  }

  op frem from FloatBinary {
    Doc "Floating-point remainder with the sign of the dividend.";
  }

  op fneg {
    Doc "Floating-point negation with optional fastmath flags (LLVM_UnaryFloatArithmeticOp, LLVMOps.td:134; record LLVM_FNegOp at LLVMOps.td:250).";
    Operands   (operand: float);
    Results    (res: float);
    Attributes (fastmathFlags: FastmathFlags = none);
    Properties [pure, same_type(operand, res)];
    Assembly   { operand if fastmathFlags { "fastmath" fastmathFlags }
                 attr-dict ":" type(res) }
  }

  op icmp {
    Doc "Integer or pointer comparison; the predicate prints through the CmpPredicate hook, operands share one type, result is i1-shaped like the operands.";
    Operands   (lhs: llvm_scalar, rhs: any);
    Results    (res: i1);
    Attributes (predicate: ICmpPredicate);
    Properties [pure, same_type(lhs, rhs)];
    Assembly   { custom<CmpPredicate>(predicate) lhs "," rhs attr-dict ":"
                 type(lhs) }
  }

  op fcmp {
    Doc "Floating-point comparison; predicate through the CmpPredicate hook, optional fastmath flags.";
    Operands   (lhs: float, rhs: float);
    Results    (res: i1);
    Attributes (predicate: FCmpPredicate, fastmathFlags: FastmathFlags = none);
    Properties [pure, same_type(lhs, rhs)];
    Assembly   { custom<CmpPredicate>(predicate) lhs "," rhs
                 if fastmathFlags { "fastmath" fastmathFlags }
                 attr-dict ":" type(lhs) }
  }

  // ---- 类型转换 ----

  schema Cast {
    Doc "Type conversion with an explicit source and target type (LLVM_CastOp, LLVMOps.td:579).";
    Operands   (arg: llvm_type);
    Results    (res: llvm_type);
    Properties [pure];
    Assembly   { arg attr-dict ":" type(arg) "to" type(res) }
  }

  schema CastWithNNeg {
    Doc "Conversion with an optional nneg marker (LLVM_CastOpWithNNegFlag, LLVMOps.td:593).";
    Operands   (arg: llvm_type);
    Results    (res: llvm_type);
    Attributes (nonNeg: optional<unit>);
    Properties [pure];
    Assembly   { if nonNeg { "nneg" } arg attr-dict ":" type(arg) "to" type(res) }
  }

  op bitcast from Cast {
    Doc "Bit-preserving conversion between non-aggregate types.";
  }
  op addrspacecast from Cast {
    Doc "Pointer conversion that changes the address space.";
  }
  op ptrtoaddr from Cast {
    Doc "Pointer-to-integer conversion that drops provenance; width follows the data layout.";
  }
  op ptrtoint from Cast {
    Doc "Pointer-to-integer conversion.";
  }
  op sext from Cast {
    Doc "Sign extension between integers of different widths.";
  }
  op sitofp from Cast {
    Doc "Signed integer to floating-point conversion.";
  }
  op fptosi from Cast {
    Doc "Floating-point to signed integer conversion (poison when out of range).";
  }
  op fptoui from Cast {
    Doc "Floating-point to unsigned integer conversion (poison when out of range).";
  }

  op zext from CastWithNNeg {
    Doc "Zero extension between integers; optional nneg promises the input is non-negative.";
  }
  op uitofp from CastWithNNeg {
    Doc "Unsigned integer to floating-point conversion; optional nneg.";
  }

  op trunc {
    Doc "Integer truncation; optional nuw/nsw flags (LLVM_CastOpWithOverflowFlag, LLVMOps.td:610). The separate llvm.intr.trunc op (LLVM_FTruncOp) prints the unary-intrinsic form.";
    Operands   (arg: integer);
    Results    (res: integer);
    Attributes (overflow_flags: IntegerOverflowFlags = none);
    Properties [pure];
    Assembly   { arg if overflow_flags { overflow_flags } attr-dict ":"
                 type(arg) "to" type(res) }
  }

  op fpext {
    Doc "Floating-point extension; optional fastmath (LLVM_CastOpWithFastMathFlag, LLVMOps.td:627).";
    Operands   (arg: float);
    Results    (res: float);
    Attributes (fastmathFlags: FastmathFlags = none);
    Properties [pure];
    Assembly   { arg if fastmathFlags { "fastmath" fastmathFlags } attr-dict ":"
                 type(arg) "to" type(res) }
  }

  op fptrunc {
    Doc "Floating-point truncation; optional fastmath.";
    Operands   (arg: float);
    Results    (res: float);
    Attributes (fastmathFlags: FastmathFlags = none);
    Properties [pure];
    Assembly   { arg if fastmathFlags { "fastmath" fastmathFlags } attr-dict ":"
                 type(arg) "to" type(res) }
  }

  op inttoptr {
    Doc "Integer to pointer conversion with an optional dereferenceable byte count (LLVM_DereferenceableCastOp, LLVMOps.td:647).";
    Operands   (arg: integer);
    Results    (res: llvm_ptr);
    Attributes (dereferenceable: optional<attribute>);
    Properties [pure];
    Assembly   { arg if dereferenceable { "dereferenceable" dereferenceable }
                 attr-dict ":" type(arg) "to" type(res) }
  }

  enum ICmpPredicate {
    Doc "Integer comparison predicates for llvm.icmp.";
    Cases [ eq = 0, ne = 1, slt = 2, sle = 3, sgt = 4, sge = 5,
            ult = 6, ule = 7, ugt = 8, uge = 9 ];
  }

  enum FCmpPredicate {
    Doc "Floating-point comparison predicates for llvm.fcmp.";
    Cases [ _false = 0, oeq = 1, ogt = 2, oge = 3, olt = 4, ole = 5, one = 6,
             ord = 7, ueq = 8, ugt = 9, uge = 10, ult = 11, ule = 12,
             une = 13, uno = 14, _true = 15 ];
  }

  enum GEPNoWrapFlags: bits {
    Doc "getelementptr no-wrap flags; inbounds implies nusw.";
    Cases [ none = 0, inbounds_flag = 1, nusw = 2, nuw = 4 ];
    Groups [ inbounds = inbounds_flag | nusw ];
  }

  // ---- 内存 ----

  op alloca {
    Doc "Stack allocation; prints through the upstream hand-written printer/parser (LLVMOps.td:296). arraySize is in elements of elem_type, alignment is optional, inalloca marks a used-with-inalloca alloca.";
    Operands   (arraySize: integer);
    Results    (res: ptr);
    Attributes (alignment: optional<i64>, elem_type: type, inalloca: optional<unit>);
    Properties [memory_effect(allocate)];
    Assembly   Custom;
  }

  op getelementptr {
    Doc "Pointer arithmetic mirroring LLVM getelementptr; the index list prints through the GEPIndices hook, elem_type is the pointee type and inrange is the constant-range qualifier (LLVMOps.td:301).";
    Operands   (base: llvm_ptr, dynamicIndices: variadic<integer>,
                operands: variadic<llvm_type>);
    Results    (res: llvm_ptr, results: variadic<llvm_type>);
    Attributes (rawConstantIndices: array<i32>, elem_type: type,
                noWrapFlags: GEPNoWrapFlags = none,
                inrange: optional<attribute>);
    Properties [pure];
    Assembly   { if noWrapFlags { noWrapFlags }
                 if inrange { "inrange" inrange }
                 base "[" custom<GEPIndices>(dynamicIndices, rawConstantIndices) "]"
                 attr-dict ":" functional-type(operands, results)
                 "," elem_type }
  }

  op load {
    Doc "Load from a pointer; volatile/atomic/nontemporal/invariant/dereferenceable/noundef/range qualifiers print in a fixed order, properties carry the memory effects (LLVMOps.td:388).";
    Operands   (addr: llvm_ptr);
    Results    (res: llvm_type);
    Attributes (alignment: optional<i64>, volatile_: optional<unit>,
                nontemporal: optional<unit>, invariant: optional<unit>,
                invariantGroup: optional<unit>,
                ordering: AtomicOrdering = not_atomic,
                syncscope: optional<string>,
                dereferenceable: optional<attribute>, noundef: optional<unit>,
                range: optional<attribute>);
    Properties [memory_effect(read)];
    Assembly   { if volatile_ { "volatile" } addr
                 if ordering { "atomic"
                               if syncscope { "syncscope" "(" syncscope ")" }
                               ordering }
                 oilist("invariant" invariant
                        | "invariant_group" invariantGroup
                        | "dereferenceable" dereferenceable
                        | "noundef" noundef
                        | "range" range)
                 prop-dict attr-dict ":" qualified(type(addr)) "->" type(res) }
  }

  op store {
    Doc "Store a value through a pointer; the volatile/atomic/invariant_group qualifiers print before the type list (LLVMOps.td:498).";
    Operands   (value: llvm_type, addr: llvm_ptr);
    Attributes (alignment: optional<i64>, volatile_: optional<unit>,
                nontemporal: optional<unit>, invariantGroup: optional<unit>,
                ordering: AtomicOrdering = not_atomic,
                syncscope: optional<string>);
    Properties [memory_effect(write)];
    Assembly   { if volatile_ { "volatile" } value "," addr
                 if ordering { "atomic"
                               if syncscope { "syncscope" "(" syncscope ")" }
                               ordering }
                 oilist("invariant_group" invariantGroup)
                 prop-dict attr-dict ":" type(value) ","
                 qualified(type(addr)) }
  }

  // ---- 调用 / invoke / 变参 ----

  op call {
    Doc "Call to an LLVM function, direct (@callee) or indirect (first callee_operand); prints through the upstream hand-written printer/parser (LLVMOps.td:952).";
    Operands   (callee_operands: variadic<llvm_type>);
    Results    (result: optional<llvm_type>);
    Attributes (var_callee_type: optional<type>, callee: optional<symbol_ref>,
                arg_attrs: optional<array<dictionary>>,
                res_attrs: optional<array<dictionary>>,
                fastmathFlags: FastmathFlags = none,
                CConv: CConv = C,
                TailCallKind: TailCallKind = none,
                memory_effects: optional<attribute>,
                no_inline: optional<unit>, always_inline: optional<unit>,
                inline_hint: optional<unit>);
    Properties [operand_segments_by_attribute];
    Assembly   Custom;
  }

  op invoke {
    Doc "Invoke a callee and continue at normalDest or unwindDest; both successor operand lists are separate variadic groups (LLVMOps.td:805).";
    Operands   (callee_operands: variadic<llvm_type>,
                normalDestOperands: variadic<llvm_type>,
                unwindDestOperands: variadic<llvm_type>);
    Results    (result: optional<llvm_type>);
    Successors (normalDest: successor, unwindDest: successor);
    Attributes (var_callee_type: optional<type>, callee: optional<symbol_ref>,
                arg_attrs: optional<array<dictionary>>,
                res_attrs: optional<array<dictionary>>,
                branch_weights: optional<array<i32>>, CConv: CConv = C);
    Properties [terminator, operand_segments_by_attribute];
    Assembly   Custom;
  }

  op landingpad {
    Doc "Landing pad of an exception handler; cleanup marks a cleanup clause and the variadic operands are the catch/filter clauses (LLVMOps.td:822).";
    Operands   (operands: variadic<llvm_type>);
    Results    (res: llvm_type);
    Attributes (cleanup: optional<unit>);
    Assembly   Custom;
  }

  op va_arg {
    Doc "Fetch the next variadic argument through an llvm.struct va_list pointer (LLVMOps.td:831).";
    Operands   (arg: llvm_ptr);
    Results    (res: llvm_type);
    Assembly   { arg attr-dict ":" functional-type(arg, res) }
  }

  op call_intrinsic {
    Doc "Call an llvm intrinsic by name, with optional operand bundles; prints through the upstream hand-written printer/parser (LLVMOps.td:2781).";
    Operands   (args: variadic<llvm_type>, op_bundle_operands: variadic<llvm_type>);
    Results    (results: optional<llvm_type>);
    Attributes (intrin: string, fastmathFlags: FastmathFlags = none,
                op_bundle_sizes: array<i32>,
                op_bundle_tags: optional<array<i32>>,
                arg_attrs: optional<array<dictionary>>,
                res_attrs: optional<array<dictionary>>);
    Properties [operand_segments_by_attribute];
    Assembly   Custom;
  }

  // ---- 向量 / 聚合 ----

  op extractelement {
    Doc "Extract one element of an LLVM vector at an integer index (LLVMOps.td:964).";
    Operands   (vector: vector, position: integer);
    Results    (res: llvm_type);
    Properties [pure];
    Assembly   { vector "[" position ":" type(position) "]" attr-dict ":"
                 type(vector) }
  }

  op insertelement {
    Doc "Insert a value into an LLVM vector at an integer index (LLVMOps.td:991).";
    Operands   (vector: vector, value: llvm_scalar, position: integer);
    Results    (res: vector);
    Properties [pure, same_type(res, vector)];
    Assembly   { value "," vector "[" position ":" type(position) "]" attr-dict
                 ":" type(vector) }
  }

  op shufflevector {
    Doc "Build a permutation of two vectors; the result type prints through the ShuffleType hook (LLVMOps.td:1023).";
    Operands   (v1: vector, v2: vector);
    Results    (res: vector);
    Attributes (mask: array<i32>);
    Properties [pure, same_type(v1, v2)];
    Assembly   { v1 "," v2 mask attr-dict ":" type(v1)
                 custom<ShuffleType>(ref(type(v1)), type(res), ref(mask)) }
  }

  op extractvalue {
    Doc "Extract a value from an aggregate at a constant index path; the result type prints through the InsertExtractValueElementType hook (LLVMOps.td:1063).";
    Operands   (container: aggregate);
    Results    (res: llvm_type);
    Attributes (position: array<i64>);
    Properties [pure];
    Assembly   { container position attr-dict ":" type(container)
                 custom<InsertExtractValueElementType>(type(res),
                                                      ref(type(container)),
                                                      ref(position)) }
  }

  op insertvalue {
    Doc "Insert a value into an aggregate at a constant index path; the container and result share a type (LLVMOps.td:1097).";
    Operands   (container: aggregate, value: llvm_scalar);
    Results    (res: aggregate);
    Attributes (position: array<i64>);
    Properties [pure, same_type(container, res)];
    Assembly   { value "," container position attr-dict ":" type(container)
                 custom<InsertExtractValueElementType>(type(value),
                                                      ref(type(container)),
                                                      ref(position)) }
  }

  // ---- 杂项 ----

  op select {
    Doc "Select between two values on a boolean (or boolean vector); trueValue, falseValue and res share a type, optional fastmath (LLVMOps.td:1129).";
    Operands   (condition: any, trueValue: llvm_type, falseValue: llvm_type);
    Results    (res: llvm_type);
    Attributes (fastmathFlags: FastmathFlags = none);
    Properties [pure, same_type(trueValue, res), same_type(falseValue, res)];
    Assembly   { operands if fastmathFlags { "fastmath" fastmathFlags }
                 attr-dict ":" type(condition) "," type(res) }
  }

  op freeze {
    Doc "Freeze a poison value into an arbitrary but fixed value (LLVMOps.td:1151).";
    Operands   (val: llvm_type);
    Results    (res: llvm_type);
    Properties [pure, same_type(val, res)];
    Assembly   { val attr-dict ":" type(val) }
  }

  // ---- 终结符 ----

  op br {
    Doc "Unconditional branch with an optional loop annotation (LLVM_TerminatorOp, LLVMOps.td:1166).";
    Operands   (destOperands: variadic<llvm_type>);
    Successors (dest: successor);
    Attributes (loop_annotation: optional<attribute>);
    Properties [terminator, pure];
    Assembly   { dest
                 if destOperands { "(" destOperands ":" type(destOperands) ")" }
                 if loop_annotation { "loop_annotation" "=" loop_annotation }
                 attr-dict }
  }

  op cond_br {
    Doc "Conditional branch with optional branch weights and per-successor operand lists (LLVMOps.td:1194).";
    Operands   (condition: i1, trueDestOperands: variadic<llvm_type>,
                falseDestOperands: variadic<llvm_type>);
    Successors (trueDest: successor, falseDest: successor);
    Attributes (branch_weights: optional<array<i32>>,
                loop_annotation: optional<attribute>);
    Properties [terminator, pure, operand_segments_by_attribute];
    Assembly   { condition
                 if branch_weights { "weights" "(" branch_weights ")" } ","
                 trueDest
                 if trueDestOperands { "(" trueDestOperands ":"
                                       type(trueDestOperands) ")" } ","
                 falseDest
                 if falseDestOperands { "(" falseDestOperands ":"
                                        type(falseDestOperands) ")" }
                 if loop_annotation { "loop_annotation" "=" loop_annotation }
                 attr-dict }
  }

  op return {
    Doc "Return from an llvm.func; the optional operand prints as its own type (ReturnLike, LLVMOps.td:1243).";
    Operands   (arg: optional<llvm_type>);
    Properties [terminator, pure, return_like];
    Assembly   { attr-dict if arg { arg ":" type(arg) } }
  }

  op resume {
    Doc "Resume unwinding with an exception value (LLVMOps.td:1271).";
    Operands   (value: llvm_type);
    Properties [terminator];
    Assembly   { value attr-dict ":" type(value) }
  }

  op unreachable {
    Doc "Terminates the block with undefined behavior if reached (LLVMOps.td:1282).";
    Properties [terminator];
    Assembly   { attr-dict }
  }

  op switch {
    Doc "Multi-way branch; cases print through the SwitchOpCases hook and optional branch weights follow them (LLVMOps.td:1291).";
    Operands   (value: integer, defaultOperands: variadic<llvm_type>,
                caseOperands: variadic<llvm_type>);
    Successors (defaultDestination: successor,
                caseDestinations: variadic<successor>);
    Attributes (case_values: optional<attribute>,
                case_operand_segments: array<i32>,
                branch_weights: optional<array<i32>>);
    Properties [terminator, pure, operand_segments_by_attribute];
    Assembly   { value ":" type(value) "," defaultDestination
                 if defaultOperands { "(" defaultOperands ":"
                                      type(defaultOperands) ")" }
                 custom<SwitchOpCases>(ref(type(value)), case_values,
                                       caseDestinations, caseOperands,
                                       type(caseOperands))
                 if branch_weights { "weights" "(" branch_weights ")" }
                 attr-dict }
  }

  op indirectbr {
    Doc "Branch to one of a variadic successor list through an address; successors and their operands print through the IndirectBrOpSucessors hook (LLVMOps.td:2004).";
    Operands   (addr: llvm_ptr, succOperands: variadic<llvm_type>);
    Successors (successor_list: variadic<successor>);
    Attributes (indbr_operand_segments: array<i32>);
    Properties [terminator, operand_segments_by_attribute];
    Assembly   { addr ":" type(addr) ","
                 custom<IndirectBrOpSucessors>(ref(type(addr)), successor_list,
                                               succOperands,
                                               type(succOperands))
                 attr-dict }
  }

  // ---- 全局值的地址与符号 ----

  op mlir.addressof {
    Doc "Pointer to a global, alias or function symbol (Pure, ConstantLike, LLVMOps.td:1370).";
    Results    (res: ptr);
    Attributes (global_name: symbol_ref);
    Properties [pure, constant_like];
    Assembly   { global_name attr-dict ":" qualified(type(res)) }
  }

  op dso_local_equivalent {
    Doc "Pointer equal to the dso_local address of a function symbol (LLVMOps.td:1884).";
    Results    (res: ptr);
    Attributes (function_name: symbol_ref);
    Properties [pure, constant_like];
    Assembly   { function_name attr-dict ":" qualified(type(res)) }
  }

  op blockaddress {
    Doc "Pointer to a basic block identified by function and tag (LLVMOps.td:1926).";
    Results    (res: ptr);
    Attributes (block_addr: attribute);
    Properties [pure, constant_like];
    Assembly   { block_addr attr-dict ":" qualified(type(res)) }
  }

  op blocktag {
    Doc "Tags the current block so that llvm.blockaddress can name it (LLVMOps.td:1972).";
    Attributes (tag: attribute);
    Assembly   { tag attr-dict }
  }

  // ---- 模块级 op ----

  op mlir.global {
    Doc "Module-level global variable with linkage, TLS mode, initializer region and optional value attribute; prints through the upstream hand-written printer/parser (LLVMOps.td:1658).";
    Regions    (initializer: region [single_block, implicit_terminator(return)]);
    Attributes (global_type: type, constant: optional<unit>, sym_name: string,
                linkage: Linkage, dso_local: optional<unit>,
                tls_mode: optional<i32>, externally_initialized: optional<unit>,
                value: optional<attribute>, alignment: optional<i64>,
                addr_space: i32 = 0, unnamed_addr: optional<UnnamedAddr>,
                visibility_: Visibility = default,
                sym_visibility: optional<string>);
    Properties [symbol, symbol_visibility, isolated_from_above, single_block];
    Assembly   Custom;
  }

  op mlir.global_ctors {
    Doc "Global constructor list with priorities and associated data, translated to the global_ctors global (LLVMOps.td:1663).";
    Attributes (ctors: array<symbol_ref>, priorities: array<i32>,
                data: array<attribute>);
    Assembly   { "ctors" "=" ctors "," "priorities" "=" priorities ","
                 "data" "=" data attr-dict }
  }

  op mlir.global_dtors {
    Doc "Global destructor list with priorities and associated data (LLVMOps.td:1699).";
    Attributes (dtors: array<symbol_ref>, priorities: array<i32>,
                data: array<attribute>);
    Assembly   { "dtors" "=" dtors "," "priorities" "=" priorities ","
                 "data" "=" data attr-dict }
  }

  op mlir.alias {
    Doc "Module-level alias symbol whose initializer region yields the aliased address; prints through the upstream hand-written printer/parser (LLVMOps.td:1811).";
    Regions    (initializer: region [single_block, implicit_terminator(return)]);
    Attributes (alias_type: type, sym_name: string, linkage: Linkage,
                dso_local: optional<unit>, tls_mode: optional<i32>,
                unnamed_addr: optional<UnnamedAddr>,
                visibility_: Visibility = default,
                sym_visibility: optional<string>);
    Properties [symbol, symbol_visibility, isolated_from_above, single_block];
    Assembly   Custom;
  }

  op mlir.ifunc {
    Doc "Indirect function whose address is resolved at runtime by a resolver function (LLVMOps.td:1816).";
    Attributes (sym_name: string, i_func_type: type, resolver: symbol_ref,
                resolver_type: type, linkage: Linkage, dso_local: optional<unit>,
                address_space: i32 = 0, unnamed_addr: UnnamedAddr = none,
                visibility_: Visibility = default,
                sym_visibility: optional<string>);
    Properties [symbol, symbol_visibility, isolated_from_above];
    Assembly   { if sym_visibility { sym_visibility }
                 custom<LLVMLinkage>(linkage)
                 if visibility_ { visibility_ }
                 if unnamed_addr { unnamed_addr }
                 sym_name ":" i_func_type "," resolver_type resolver
                 oilist<",">("dso_local" dso_local
                              | "addr_space" "=" address_space)
                 attr-dict }
  }

  op comdat {
    Doc "COMDAT group region with a symbol table and no terminator (LLVMOps.td:2092).";
    Regions    (body: region [single_block, no_terminator]);
    Attributes (sym_name: string, sym_visibility: optional<string>);
    Properties [symbol, symbol_table, symbol_visibility, no_terminator,
                no_region_args];
    Assembly   { if sym_visibility { sym_visibility } sym_name body attr-dict }
  }

  op comdat_selector {
    Doc "Declaration of one COMDAT selector inside an llvm.comdat group (LLVMOps.td:2068).";
    Attributes (sym_name: string, comdat: string,
                sym_visibility: optional<string>);
    Properties [symbol, symbol_visibility];
    Assembly   { if sym_visibility { sym_visibility } sym_name comdat attr-dict }
  }

  op func {
    Doc "LLVM function definition or declaration with linkage, calling convention, comdat and personality; prints through the upstream hand-written printer/parser (LLVMOps.td:2274).";
    Regions    (body: region);
    Attributes (sym_name: string, sym_visibility: optional<string>,
                function_type: type, linkage: Linkage = external,
                dso_local: optional<unit>, CConv: CConv = C,
                comdat: optional<symbol_ref>, convergent: optional<unit>,
                personality: optional<symbol_ref>,
                garbageCollector: optional<string>,
                passthrough: optional<array<attribute>>,
                arg_attrs: optional<array<dictionary>>,
                res_attrs: optional<array<dictionary>>,
                function_entry_count: optional<attribute>,
                use_sample_profile: optional<bool>,
                disable_tail_calls: optional<bool>);
    Properties [symbol, symbol_visibility, isolated_from_above, affine_scope,
                automatic_allocation_scope];
    Assembly   Custom;
  }

  // ---- 常量 ----

  op mlir.none {
    Doc "The LLVM none token literal as a !token SSA value (LLVMOps.td:2281).";
    Results    (res: token);
    Properties [pure];
    Assembly   { attr-dict ":" type(res) }
  }

  op mlir.undef {
    Doc "Value of an LLVM type that is undef, as opposed to the less-defined poison (LLVMOps.td:2305).";
    Results    (res: llvm_type);
    Properties [pure, constant_like];
    Assembly   { attr-dict ":" type(res) }
  }

  op mlir.poison {
    Doc "Value of an LLVM type that is poison (LLVMOps.td:2327).";
    Results    (res: llvm_type);
    Properties [pure, constant_like];
    Assembly   { attr-dict ":" type(res) }
  }

  op mlir.zero {
    Doc "The zeroinitializer constant of an LLVM type (LLVMOps.td:2350).";
    Results    (res: llvm_type);
    Properties [pure, constant_like];
    Assembly   { attr-dict ":" type(res) }
  }

  op mlir.constant {
    Doc "Literal constant given as an attribute in parentheses and typed by the result (LLVMOps.td:2376).";
    Results    (res: llvm_type);
    Attributes (value: attribute);
    Properties [pure, constant_like];
    Assembly   { "(" value ")" attr-dict ":" type(res) }
  }

  op mlir.metadata_as_value {
    Doc "Wraps an LLVM metadata constant so it can be used as an SSA value (LLVMOps.td:2687).";
    Results    (res: metadata);
    Attributes (metadata: attribute);
    Properties [pure, constant_like];
    Assembly   { metadata attr-dict }
  }

  // ---- 原子 / 内存序 ----

  op atomicrmw {
    Doc "Atomic read-modify-write of a pointer location; the bin_op selects the operation and the result shares the value type (LLVMOps.td:2486).";
    Operands   (ptr: llvm_ptr, val: llvm_type);
    Results    (res: llvm_type);
    Attributes (bin_op: AtomicBinOp,
                ordering: AtomicOrdering = seq_cst,
                syncscope: optional<string>, alignment: optional<i64>,
                volatile_: optional<unit>, ignore_denormal_mode: optional<unit>);
    Assembly   { if volatile_ { "volatile" }
                 if ignore_denormal_mode { "ignore_denormal_mode" }
                 bin_op ptr "," val
                 if syncscope { "syncscope" "(" syncscope ")" }
                 ordering prop-dict attr-dict ":" qualified(type(ptr)) ","
                 type(val) }
  }

  op cmpxchg {
    Doc "Atomic compare-and-exchange; val and cmp share a type and the result is the {T, i1} struct (LLVMOps.td:2552).";
    Operands   (ptr: llvm_ptr, cmp: llvm_type, val: llvm_type);
    Results    (res: struct);
    Attributes (success_ordering: AtomicOrdering = seq_cst,
                failure_ordering: AtomicOrdering = seq_cst,
                syncscope: optional<string>, alignment: optional<i64>,
                weak: optional<unit>, volatile_: optional<unit>);
    Properties [same_type(cmp, val)];
    Assembly   { if weak { "weak" } if volatile_ { "volatile" }
                 ptr "," cmp "," val
                 if syncscope { "syncscope" "(" syncscope ")" }
                 success_ordering failure_ordering prop-dict attr-dict ":"
                 qualified(type(ptr)) "," type(val) }
  }

  op fence {
    Doc "Memory fence with an ordering and an optional syncscope (LLVMOps.td:2610).";
    Attributes (ordering: AtomicOrdering = seq_cst,
                syncscope: optional<string>);
    Assembly   { if syncscope { "syncscope" "(" syncscope ")" } ordering
                 attr-dict }
  }

  op inline_asm {
    Doc "Inline assembly call; the qualifier prefix and the operand list print before the functional type (LLVMOps.td:2635).";
    Operands   (operands: variadic<llvm_type>);
    Results    (res: optional<llvm_type>);
    Attributes (asm_string: string, constraints: string,
                has_side_effects: optional<unit>, is_align_stack: optional<unit>,
                tail_call_kind: TailCallKind = none, convergent: optional<unit>,
                asm_dialect: optional<i32>,
                operand_attrs: optional<array<attribute>>);
    Assembly   { if has_side_effects { "has_side_effects" }
                 if is_align_stack { "is_align_stack" }
                 if tail_call_kind { "tail_call_kind" "=" tail_call_kind }
                 if convergent { "convergent" }
                 if asm_dialect { "asm_dialect" "=" asm_dialect }
                 if operand_attrs { "operand_attrs" "=" operand_attrs }
                 attr-dict asm_string "," constraints operands ":"
                 functional-type(operands, results) }
  }

  op linker_options {
    Doc "Options passed to the linker for the produced object file (LLVMOps.td:2794).";
    Attributes (options: array<string>);
    Assembly   { options attr-dict }
  }

  op module_flags {
    Doc "Module flags translated to llvm.module.flags metadata triplets (LLVMOps.td:2827).";
    Attributes (flags: array<attribute>);
    Assembly   { flags attr-dict }
  }

  op named_metadata {
    Doc "Module-level named metadata node holding a list of metadata nodes (LLVMOps.td:2861).";
    Attributes (metadata_name: string, nodes: array<attribute>);
    Assembly   { metadata_name nodes attr-dict }
  }

  // ---- intrinsic 骨架 ----

  schema Intrinsic {
    Doc "Intrinsic with all operands and results of one LLVM type: `(operands) attr-dict : functional-type(operands, results)` (LLVM_UnaryIntrOpBase / LLVM_BinarySameArgsIntrOpBase / LLVM_TernarySameArgsIntrOpBase, LLVMIntrinsicOps.td:16-94).";
    Operands   (operands: variadic<llvm_type>);
    Results    (results: variadic<llvm_type>);
    Properties [pure, same_type(operands, results)];
    Assembly   { "(" operands ")" attr-dict ":"
                 functional-type(operands, results) }
  }

  schema IntrinsicPure {
    Doc "Intrinsic with the plain operand/result text but without the same-type guarantee: `(operands) attr-dict : functional-type(operands, results)` (LLVM_IntRoundIntrOpBase, LLVM_CmpIntrOp, LLVMIntrinsicOps.td:191-205, 232).";
    Operands   (operands: variadic<llvm_type>);
    Results    (results: variadic<llvm_type>);
    Properties [pure];
    Assembly   { "(" operands ")" attr-dict ":"
                 functional-type(operands, results) }
  }

  schema IntrinsicWithFastmathPure {
    Doc "Same text as IntrinsicWithFastmath but only Pure is guaranteed (LLVM_PowIOp, LLVM_IntRoundIntrOpBase, LLVMIntrinsicOps.td:178-205).";
    Operands   (operands: variadic<llvm_type>);
    Results    (results: variadic<llvm_type>);
    Attributes (fastmathFlags: FastmathFlags = none);
    Properties [pure];
    Assembly   { "(" operands ")"
                 if fastmathFlags { "fastmath" fastmathFlags }
                 attr-dict ":" functional-type(operands, results) }
  }

  schema IntrinsicWithFastmath {
    Doc "Same shape as Intrinsic plus an optional `fastmath` flags group (LLVM_UnaryIntrOpF and friends, LLVMIntrinsicOps.td:32-66).";
    Operands   (operands: variadic<llvm_type>);
    Results    (results: variadic<llvm_type>);
    Attributes (fastmathFlags: FastmathFlags = none);
    Properties [pure, same_type(operands, results)];
    Assembly   { "(" operands ")"
                 if fastmathFlags { "fastmath" fastmathFlags }
                 attr-dict ":" functional-type(operands, results) }
  }

  schema TwoResultIntrinsic {
    Doc "Two-result float intrinsic (frexp/sincos/modf); the fastmath group prints between the operand list and attr-dict (LLVM_TwoResultIntrOp, LLVMIntrinsicOps.td:68-94).";
    Operands   (operands: variadic<llvm_type>);
    Results    (results: variadic<llvm_type>);
    Attributes (fastmathFlags: FastmathFlags = none);
    Properties [pure];
    Assembly   { "(" operands ")"
                 if fastmathFlags { "fastmath" fastmathFlags }
                 attr-dict ":" functional-type(operands, results) }
  }

  schema MaskedLoadLike {
    Doc "Masked load/gather: operand list, optional alignment, printed properties, then the functional type (LLVM_MaskedLoadOp/LLVM_masked_gather, LLVMIntrinsicOps.td:1096-1145).";
    Operands   (operands: variadic<llvm_type>);
    Results    (results: variadic<llvm_type>);
    Attributes (alignment: optional<i64>);
    Assembly   { "(" operands ")"
                 if alignment { "," "alignment" "(" alignment ")" }
                 prop-dict attr-dict ":"
                 functional-type(operands, results) }
  }

